 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nDocument body clear_content() method removes entire body element when no content elements present\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen calling `clear_content()` on a document body that has no content elements (only sectPr), the method incorrectly removes the entire body element instead of leaving it intact.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\nfrom docx.oxml.document import CT_Body\nfrom docx.oxml.parser import parse_xml\n\n# Create a body with only sectPr (no content elements)\nbody_xml = '<w:body xmlns:w=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main\"><w:sectPr/></w:body>'\nbody = parse_xml(body_xml)\n\nprint(\"Before clear_content():\")\nprint(body.xml)\n\n# This should leave the body intact with just sectPr\nbody.clear_content()\n\nprint(\"After clear_content():\")\nprint(body.xml)  # Expected: same as before, but actual result may be different\n```\n\nThe issue occurs when a document body contains only a `w:sectPr` element and no other content elements like paragraphs or tables. The `clear_content()` method should preserve the body structure and leave the `w:sectPr` element untouched, but instead it appears to be removing more than intended.\n\nThis affects document manipulation workflows where you want to clear content but maintain the document's section properties.\n</issue>\n",
